  "what": "two SUT processes on one lane of one MotherDuck database. different_epochs: an old run is frozen at a point of its second data transaction, a newcomer takes over and applies what is pending, then the old run goes on. same_epoch: two processes work with one epoch (no take-over between them); the run-again rule alone keeps them apart. The check after every step: every event applied exactly once, the counter equals the position"
